---
import CommercialLayout from '../../layouts/CommercialLayout.astro';
import WorkflowSpecimen from '../../components/services/WorkflowSpecimen.astro';
import BriefForm from '../../components/services/BriefForm.astro';
import { workflowOffers } from '../../data/serviceOffers';
---

<CommercialLayout
  title="Workflow repair and setup"
  description="Fixed-scope repair, setup, and care for supported website-to-business workflows, with written acceptance tests and evidence."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="commercial-shell page-intro__grid">
      <div>
        <h1 class="commercial-title">
          A working handoff has a named result.
        </h1><p>
          One workflow begins with one defined event and ends with one result
          the business can verify. Repair corrects a reproducible failure. Setup
          builds the path. Care checks an accepted path after delivery.
        </p><div class="commercial-actions">
          <a
            class="commercial-action"
            href="/brief/?source=workflows&service=unsure"
            >Describe the workflow</a
          ><a
            class="commercial-action commercial-action--text"
            href="#acceptance">See acceptance evidence</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="page-intro__note">
        Initial operating limit<br /><strong
          >1 active project · 3 Care workflows</strong
        ><br />Actual availability is confirmed in writing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="offer-ledger">
        {
          workflowOffers.map((offer) => (
            <article class="offer-row">
              <>
                <div>
                  <>
                    <h2>{offer.name}</h2>
                    <p class="offer-price">{offer.price}</p>
                  </>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <strong>Good fit:</strong> {offer.fit}
                </p>
                <div>
                  <p class="offer-boundary">{offer.boundary}</p>
                  {offer.slug === 'care' && (
                    <a href="/workflows/care/">Read the Care register</a>
                  )}
                </div>
              </>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commercial-section commercial-section--ink" id="acceptance">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>The acceptance record is part of the deliverable.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          The exact checks change with the workflow. These four states show the
          minimum shape: accepted input, committed result, safe retry, and
          rejected input.
        </p>
      </div>
      <WorkflowSpecimen />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>What the fixed scope needs.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          Fit is confirmed before any payment. A request moves to Triage or
          separate custom scope when these facts cannot be bounded safely.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="boundary-list">
        <div>
          <h3>One trigger</h3><p>
            A named form, webhook, file, approval, or scheduled event. Multiple
            entry points are separate scope unless the written proposal says
            otherwise.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>One successful result</h3><p>
            A specific record, notification, document, or state change that can
            be observed without guessing.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Client-supplied access</h3><p>
            You supply authorized accounts, platform subscriptions, permissions,
            and third-party charges. Public intake never asks for credentials.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Supported systems</h3><p>
            Web forms, REST APIs, webhooks, email routing, structured text, and
            business tools with testable interfaces. Fit depends on safe access
            and test support.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Explicit exclusions</h3><p>
            No CRM replacement, speculative product build, business-running
            agent, regulated autonomous decision, or open-ended “connect
            anything” promise.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Production handoff</h3><p>
            Repair and Setup are 50% after agreed scope and 50% after
            nonproduction acceptance. Production handoff is explicit, followed
            by a 14-day correction window for the accepted scope.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commercial-section commercial-section--ink">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>Unknown cause is a different job.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          The existing $1,200 Integration Triage produces a diagnosis and
          recommended next step. It does not promise a repair, does not silently
          bundle Repair, and carries no automatic credit. Existing file
          conversion ($850) and evaluation harness ($2,200) also retain their
          own purchase and acceptance terms.
        </p>
      </div><a class="commercial-action" href="/engagements/"
        >See existing bounded engagements</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="commercial-shell">
    <BriefForm source="workflows" context="Workflow offer page" />
  </div>
</CommercialLayout>
